Mongoose, vendored
==================

  https://github.com/cesanta/mongoose
  version 7.23

Two files, taken from upstream and never edited: mongoose.c and
mongoose.h, the amalgamation upstream publishes and supports.  Updating
means replacing both and running the tests; there is no patch to carry
forward, and there must never be one -- the reason to use this instead of
the hand-written server it replaced is that it is somebody else's tested
code, and a local edit gives that away.

The build compiles mongoose.c with its own definitions (see
ircd/CMakeLists.txt) and nothing else in the tree includes mongoose.h
except ircd/http_server.c, which is the only file that knows this library
exists.  Everything else sees include/http.h.

LICENCE
-------

Mongoose is GPL-2.0-only, or a commercial licence from Cesanta.  ircu2 is
GPL-2.0-or-later, and code offered under "version 2 or any later version"
may be used under version 2, so the combined work is distributable under
GPL-2.0.  What that costs is the "or later": an ircd built with Mongoose
in it is GPL-2.0-only.

If that is not acceptable for a given deployment, the answer is a
commercial licence from Cesanta -- not a fork of this file.
